Match_Dop. Let $A$ be an element of $\mathrm{Set}$. Let $\mathrm{\_nil}$ be an element of $A$. Let $\mathrm{return\_sort}$ be an element of $\mathrm{Sort}$. Let $\mathrm{return\_type}$ be a function from elements $z$ of $\mathrm{Dop}$ applied to $A$ and $\mathrm{\_nil}$ to elements of $\mathrm{return\_sort}$. Let $\mathrm{case\_mk\_Dop}$ be a function from elements $\mathrm{sum}$ of $\mathrm{ACop}$ applied to $A$ and $\mathrm{\_nil}$ and functions $\mathrm{prod}$ from elements of $A$ and elements $\mathrm{\_\_1}$ of $A$ to elements of $A$ and functions $\mathrm{\_null}$ from elements $a$ of $A$ to elements of $\mathrm{Eq}$ applied to $\mathrm{prod}$ applied to $a$ and $\mathrm{\_nil}$ and $\mathrm{\_nil}$ and functions $\mathrm{\_distr}$ from elements $a$ of $A$ and elements $b$ of $A$ and elements $c$ of $A$ to elements of $\mathrm{Eq}$ applied to $\mathrm{prod}$ applied to $a$ and $\mathrm{aop\_\_o\_\_op}$ applied to $A$, $\mathrm{\_nil}$, $\mathrm{sum}$, $b$ and $c$ and $\mathrm{aop\_\_o\_\_op}$ applied to $A$, $\mathrm{\_nil}$, $\mathrm{sum}$, $\mathrm{prod}$ applied to $a$ and $b$ and $\mathrm{prod}$ applied to $a$ and $c$ to elements of $\mathrm{return\_type}$ applied to $\mathrm{mk\_Dop}$ applied to $A$, $\mathrm{\_nil}$, $\mathrm{sum}$, $\mathrm{prod}$, $\mathrm{\_null}$ and $\mathrm{\_distr}$. Let $z$ be an element of $\mathrm{Dop}$ applied to $A$ and $\mathrm{\_nil}$. Then $\mathrm{return\_type}$ holds for $z$.
